Split GPU thread: the MME's DMA reads (Maxwell3D::FrontDmaRead) read guest memory ahead of the work
queued for the back, as the hardware's front end does.
(ProsperoEden eglantine-a42b4d4-ps5.d 0022 mme-dma-read-ahead, 0024 pending-report-writes,
0026 dma-read-trust with 0030 dma-read-trust-opt-in, and 0032's EverReported test; adapted to
EglantinePS5, whose read also flushes the query cache.)

A read drains the back (then asks its buffer and query caches for what the GPU wrote) only after a
wait for idle, 3D or puller, since the last drain (GpuSplit::NoteSync, SyncPending), for reads
longer than 64 words, or when one of its words is still to be written by the back (a 3D report or
a release the front sent: GpuSplit::NoteReport, WritePending) or ever had a report sent to it (its
result can wait in the query cache, GpuSplit::EverReported). Draining for every read cost the
front about a quarter of each second in races; the reads the drain changed were reports the back
had not written yet. EDEN_NX2_DMA_READ_AHEAD=0 drains for every read again.
EDEN_NX2_DMA_READ_TRUST=1 (opt-in) also reads ahead after a wait for idle from sources whose last
16 drains found nothing new (two races ended in GPU page faults with it in ProsperoEden).

